Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:30:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] MT-E2: Motor Test -- the no-decision golden functions
 (select, cell edit, Copy From, speed bar, loop timing, LastHomePos, Reload
 re-applies Mot_Table)

Every Motor Test control that needed no user ruling, each against golden uMotorTest.cpp:
- selectMotor (lM00Click/lpA00Click :734-790): Enable=0 refused before anything (golden :740-743); AllBtnUp;
  MOT.SetSpeed(1) -> 1% PTP speeds to a 1203 card as golden would; runtime.selectedMotor.
- setParamCell (SelectCell :1176-1222), copyFrom (BitBtn1Click :1384-1401), setSpeed (scroll bar :791-810 jog+PTP,
  edtSpeedChange :1587-1603 PTP only; Index axes nothing). Jog = golden: the last scroll-bar jog % of that axis,
  1% until the bar moves.
- runtime per motor "cur" (golden UpdateMotorParameter rows + ReadRate/ReadRange/GetSpeed/LastHomePos), motion
  jogPTime/jogNTime/avgTime (golden lblJogPTime/lblJogNTime/lblAvgTime semantics, arrival checked after every
  1203 Poll via W906_MotorAccessPollTick, QPC).
- Alarm rule of UpdateMotorLed (:644-652) at the moment an alarm is raised; LastHomePos recorded on home end.
- Reload Motor Data re-reads Mot_Table.csv (read only) and re-applies the InitialMotorParameter table values to the
  existing MOT[i].Motor objects in place; rows whose identity changed are skipped ("restart wb_serve").
Tests: WebMotorAccess 278/0, MotorPoints_HT9050 54/54; control gate only the pre-existing START_RING FAIL;
readonly gate PASS; pe_truncation PASS; production_audit 0 changes. Not yet run on the machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
